      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the degree measure of an angle whose measure is double the measure of its complement, we start by defining the angle and its complement.\n\n1. Let the measure of the angle be \\( x \\) degrees.\n2. The complement of an angle is \\( 90^\\circ - x \\) degrees.\n\nAccording to the problem, the measure of the angle is double the measure of its complement. Therefore, we can write the equation:\n\\[ x = 2(90^\\circ - x) \\]\n\n3. Next, we solve for \\( x \\):\n\\[ x = 180^\\circ - 2x \\]\n\\[ x + 2x = 180^\\circ \\]\n\\[ 3x = 180^\\circ \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{180^\\circ}{3} \\]\n\\[ x = 60^\\circ \\]\n\nSo, the measure of the angle is \\( 60^\\circ \\).\n\n4. To verify, we check if the complement of \\( 60^\\circ \\) is indeed \\( 90^\\circ - 60^\\circ = 30^\\circ \\), and \\( 60^\\circ \\) is double \\( 30^\\circ \\):\n\\[ 60^\\circ = 2 \\times 30^\\circ \\]\n\nThe solution is correct. Therefore, the degree measure of the angle is \\(\\boxed{60}\\).",
