      "text": "To find the degree measure of an angle whose measure is double the measure of its complement, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Let \\( x \\) be the measure of the angle.\n2. The complement of the angle is \\( 90^\\circ - x \\).\n3. According to the problem, the angle is double its complement, so we can write the equation:\n   \\[\n   x = 2(90^\\circ - x)\n   \\]\n4. Simplify the equation:\n   \\[\n   x = 180^\\circ - 2x\n   \\]\n5. Add \\( 2x \\) to both sides to combine like terms:\n   \\[\n   x + 2x = 180^\\circ\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   3x = 180^\\circ\n   \\]\n6. Divide both sides by 3 to solve for \\( x \\):\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{180^\\circ}{3} = 60^\\circ\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the degree measure of the angle is \\(\\boxed{60}\\).",
